---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Gaming · Ironfeast">
  <section class="about container gaming-about">
    <h2>IRONFEAST ENTERTAINMENT</h2>
    <p class="sub">Strategy. Simulation. Systemic Mastery.</p>

    <div class="about-body">
      <p>
        We do not just play; we engineer solutions. From the macroeconomic
        management of Roman currency to the logistical complexities of factory
        automation, Ironfeast offers a cerebral approach to high-fidelity
        gaming.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="gaming-section">
    <div class="game">
      <h3>🏛️ ANNO 117: PAX ROMANA</h3>
      <div class="desc">
        <strong>The Macroeconomic Framework</strong> — Move beyond basic city-building
        into true empire management. Our Anno 117 content focuses on long-term efficiency
        and military technology optimization.
      </div>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Featured Guide:</strong> The Repair Crane Strategy — Naval warfare
          is essential for protecting trade routes, but constant repairs drain the
          treasury. Our latest analysis demonstrates how unlocking the Repair Crane
          via the military technology tree and placing it strategically near naval
          bases ensures automated, rapid fleet recovery. Doctrine: "Never Lose a Ship".
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>The "Denarius" Philosophy:</strong> Treat the game as a complex
          economic simulation requiring strict fiscal discipline and long-term resource
          forecasting.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="cta-links">
        [<a href="https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLb4KpjqJg2Rj-ekGWNHpor4h6J5fedbj2">Watch the Strategy Guides</a>] | [<a
          href="https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLb4KpjqJg2RhilyFpQXbPFmd6-ixQVGfz">View the VOD Archive</a
        >]
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="game">
      <h3>⚙️ FACTORIO &amp; AUTOMATION ROOTS</h3>
      <div class="desc">
        <strong>The Foundation of "Lead Cap" Engineering</strong> — The channel's
        dedication to automation runs deep, tracing back to the "Lead Cap" era. This
        vertical represents the purest form of our "systems-first" philosophy.
      </div>
      <ul>
        <li>
          The Optimization Loop: supply chain optimization and throughput
          analysis for solo and multiplayer.
        </li>
        <li>
          Cross-Pollination: Factorio logic (bus balancing, bottleneck analysis)
          applied to other technical modpacks.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="cta-links">
        [<a href="https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLb4KpjqJg2RjQRZR-XGhufzhaIykYAT00">Death World Experience</a>] | [<a
          href="https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLb4KpjqJg2RjUz7nEXBFo65opsU8cFxK-">To the Edge and Back</a>]
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="game">
      <h3>⛏️ VINTAGE STORY</h3>
      <div class="desc">
        <strong>Scientific Realism &amp; Geological Survival</strong> — A chronicle
        of evolution, focusing on granular mechanics and infrastructure development.
      </div>
      <ul>
        <li>
          The Survival Logs: follow progression from scratch (e.g., Day 3
          milestone: the struggle for the "First Meal").
        </li>
        <li>
          Infrastructure: beehive kilns and road systems for efficient travel
          across complex terrain.
        </li>
        <li>
          Community Operations: collaborative server applying survival
          principles.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="cta-links">
        [<a href="https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLb4KpjqJg2RgyyYGECdUV--3_fYOC6LM9">First ever look at the game</a>] | [<a
          href="https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLb4KpjqJg2Rhh5CqCAyaF8M_VYvLkbKOA">Community server</a>]
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="game">
      <h3>🧱 STONEBLOCK 4</h3>
      <div class="desc">
        <strong>The Engineer's Silo</strong> — Remodeling survival into a "Silo-themed"
        vertical base structure, applying architectural engineering to a world of
        stone.
      </div>
      <ul>
        <li>
          The Silo Project: agricultural and industrial levels, automated
          Cloches, and centralized Applied Energistics.
        </li>
        <li>
          The World Engine: endgame objective requiring complex multiblock
          automation.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="cta-links">
        [<a href="https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLb4KpjqJg2RiWc-SHAIA0k-DIGXDZr5sn">The Silo Project</a>]
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="game">
      <h3>🌱 VARIETY: LIGHTYEAR FRONTIER</h3>
      <div class="desc">
        <strong>The "Cozy-Hardcore" Hybrid</strong> — Applying rigorous workflows
        to Cozy Mech Farming: mech optimization, irrigation, and restoration mechanics.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="game">
      <h3>📜 THE ORIGINS</h3>
      <div class="desc">
        <strong>From Paladin to Engineer</strong> — The "Ironfeast" identity began
        as a protective role (Paladin) in WoW and evolved into Digital Engineering.
        We use professional tools and AI (Copilot) to produce high-fidelity content.
      </div>
      <p class="cta-links">
        [<a href="/community/discord/">Join the Discord Community</a>] | [<a
          href="https://www.twitch.tv/ironfeast">Live on Twitch</a
        >]
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
